From ef47116176cefc7a2ad04952b916585edc71b19d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 01:36:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 57/58] engine, executor: drain-order shutdown

- EngineCore survives a late SIGTERM during teardown (bounded deferral) so
  every worker drains its guard telemetry.
- A worker exits right after its orderly shutdown.
- A worker failure racing shutdown stays a failure (exit 1).
- Rank 0 waits for the PLE child's whole thread group, bounded, instead of its
  reap; drain-aware failure ladder with a bounded grace for survivors whose
  shutdown already started.
- tests: the sorted-emit graph arm takes max_len on the host before capture.
